# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FAERS Signal Detection
#
# Rule of thumb: anything that can be regenerated from sas/ plus the raw FDA
# extract stays out of version control. Anything that documents a decision or
# proves data quality goes in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Raw FAERS ASCII extracts ---------------------------------------------
# ~1.4 GB, and published by the FDA - not ours to redistribute.
faers_ascii_*/
raw-data/

# --- Regenerable SAS output ------------------------------------------------
output/clean/
output/signal/
output/figures/
output/logs/

# output/tables/ uses the /* form, not a trailing slash: git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so 'output/tables/' would make the
# negations below dead rules. Same pattern as output/csv/* further down.
#
# What stays out: the intermediate result sets, led by signals_ebgm.csv (24 MB)
# and all_signals_flagged.csv (20 MB). They are regenerated by a rerun, and
# storing every version of them would bloat the clone for no benefit.
#
# What comes in: the control results and the 10 report_*.csv tables, 112 KB in
# total. Every figure quoted in README.md and portfolio/CASE_STUDY.md is read
# from those tables, so a reader can check the numbers against their source.
output/tables/*
!output/tables/positive_controls.csv
!output/tables/negative_controls.csv
!output/tables/report_*.csv

# Same categories wherever else they land
*.sas7bdat
*.log

# output/qc/*.csv is deliberately NOT ignored: those few KB are the Gate
# evidence chain (row counts, field widths, pipeline audit). Kept explicit so
# a future broad rule such as output/* cannot silently drop them.
!output/qc/*.csv

# --- Credentials - never commit -------------------------------------------
credentials.json
token*.json
*.env
.env
*.pem
*.key

# --- MySQL load staging ----------------------------------------------------
# Mirrors the SAS ODA layout: what 01b_export_csv.sas writes to output/csv/
# there is downloaded to output/csv/ here. Roughly 2 GB, fully regenerable.
# The directory itself stays in the repo because sql/02_load.sql resolves its
# path with $(pwd).
output/csv/*
!output/csv/README.md

# --- Local databases -------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Environments and caches ----------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Tableau working files -------------------------------------------------
# Auto-save recovery files. Tableau writes a new one every time the workbook
# is open and deletes them on a clean exit, so they are pure session noise.
.~*.twbr

# The workbook itself is published to Tableau Public, which is the canonical
# copy and the only one a reader can interact with. A .twb in the repo would
# be a second version to keep in step with it for no reader benefit. The
# dashboard is documented by README and portfolio/CASE_STUDY.md; the live
# version is on Tableau Public.
dashboard/*.twb

# DASHBOARD_SPEC.md is the planning document behind that build: layout
# drafts, chart-by-chart decisions and revision history. Same category as
# docs/ below - process, not product.
dashboard/DASHBOARD_SPEC.md

# --- OS cruft --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Internal working docs -------------------------------------------------
# Planning, status tracking and agent instructions. Useful locally, but they
# are process notes rather than deliverables, so they stay off the public
# repo. README.md remains the single entry point for anyone reading this
# project from the outside.
CLAUDE.md
STATUS.md
CHARTER.md

# Implementation specs handed to the coding agent, and its raw session
# output. Same reasoning as the three files above - process, not product -
# and not published while the project is still in flight.
docs/
Claude outputs/
docs/reviews/2026-09-09_independent_review.md
